I'll try a Lunar this time. Probably a No Moon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T14:56:37-08:00","id":400875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=400870#post400870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bah, I had a renegade abyssal concept I've been wanting to play. However, since you already got a possible Infernal, I'll send over a Solar Eclipse instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome everybody!<br /> <br /> What type of Renegade Abyssal? If you really want to, I'd like to see what you had in mind before whole-sale shooting it down. Lay 'em on me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T15:05:33-08:00","id":400880,"title":"","content":"Are alchemical totally out of the question ? I want to try playing one if you would allow it and yes I know of the trouble it is to play such a type of exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T15:30:27-08:00","id":400892,"title":"","content":"I just finished writing up my Eclipse background and I am kind of digging it.<br /> <br /> My Abyssal was a Midnight Shaman of the Dead. I'll save that for another game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T15:31:40-08:00","id":400895,"title":"","content":"Wait, Is this a play by post game? I don't have time for another skype game right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T15:37:32-08:00","id":400902,"title":"","content":"Oh, sorry, yes, this is a play by post game. Sorry, I ought to have said this. I'll amend the intro post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T16:02:19-08:00","id":400932,"title":"","content":"Also, sorry, Magnusar, I didn't see your last post. I'd really prefer no Alchemicals because of the huge infrastructure necesary to do them justice. If you really want to, I'll allow it and figure out something, but I'd prefer personally if there weren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T16:15:43-08:00","id":400969,"title":"","content":"So is anyone planning on going heavy combat? Just need to know how far into melee I should be (or just skip it all together). Might go thrown instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-10-2015, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T16:35:11-08:00","id":400986,"title":"","content":"I've got a Solar concept I've wanted to run for ages, namely for 3E when it comes out which thankfully we've finally entered the final stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T16:43:48-08:00","id":400993,"title":"","content":"Oh? What sort of concept do you have in mind, AkatsukiLeader13?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T16:45:08-08:00","id":400996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=400969#post400969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is anyone planning on going heavy combat? Just need to know how far into melee I should be (or just skip it all together). Might go thrown instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what you mean by heavy combat. If my Infernal is accepted there will be MHM + GSNF + various Infernal 2.5 charms which are mostly combat related.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T16:51:39-08:00","id":401000,"title":"","content":"Your Infernal WIP looks fine, Exthalion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T17:01:12-08:00","id":401024,"title":"","content":"Basically, if I only take two Thrown charms and no dodge/resistance will my character die?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T17:13:07-08:00","id":401032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=400932#post400932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, sorry, Magnusar, I didn't see your last post. I'd really prefer no Alchemicals because of the huge infrastructure necesary to do them justice. If you really want to, I'll allow it and figure out something, but I'd prefer personally if there weren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... this is a though situation I really want to play one but I don't want to screw the game so you are the final judge but the character is mostly ready so if I can play it I would like to.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T17:16:02-08:00","id":401035,"title":"","content":"A combat focus is by no means necessary. However, the Labyrinth Forest is a dangerous place, and having basic protections is highly recommended, even if I try to avoid paranoia combat as much as I can. I assume most times that characters will most all be specced to what seems right, and honestly, it just breaks my immersion if every single Exalt is a combat hobo like this is a Wuxia movie where anything is an excuse for a kung fu battle. <br /> <br /> That being said, have you played Etrian Odyssey or similar dungeon crawlers before? Because while there is definitely a place for combatants, there's also a place for diplomats, survival guides and scholars, what with the trekking through the jungle, fighting the wildlife, meeting the intelligent inhabitants, and recording discoveries. That's sort of my vision for this game, at this stage, in any case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T17:18:26-08:00","id":401056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=401032#post401032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm... this is a though situation I really want to play one but I don't want to screw the game so you are the final judge but the character is mostly ready so if I can play it I would like to.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Send me what you got in a PM, and I'll see what I can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T17:24:34-08:00","id":401061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=401000#post401000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Infernal WIP looks fine, Exthalion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much obliged.<br /> <br /> I do have two mechanical questions if you don't mind.<br /> <br /> First, is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/124885-how-to-put-a-band-aid-on-infernals?p=128384#post128384\">this set of charms/errata </a>from Vance acceptable to use?<br /> <br /> Second, if I am building a personal cult do I use the 1 free dot of cult as a base or do I have to get a second cult background?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T17:26:06-08:00","id":401062,"title":"","content":"Cool. I only took enough combat charms for someone who participated in back room dealings on the Blessed Isle. My character is totally going to be a fish out of water in this Northern Wilderness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T17:34:07-08:00","id":401089,"title":"","content":"You're wlecome, Exthalion, As per the Errata, that's fine to use Vance's fixes. His fixes are likely to be much better than mine, and in my experience, Infernals take a little bit of strategizing one's purchases to really get going, so any little extra bit helps. <br /> <br /> As per the cult, I assume that the cult goes off the inherent cult all GSPs get, so you need worry over one group of worshipful lackeys.<br /> <br /> @WonderandAwe:<br /> That's not necessarily a bad thing. You'll have a different perspective than others. I read the profile you sent me, and it looks fine, except for one thing: Which excellency did you purchase? I don't think it specified. Apart from that, it looked good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T17:45:08-08:00","id":401096,"title":"","content":"Bureaucracy. Anathema does them weird. There is a little tables with dots above the charm listing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T17:49:35-08:00","id":401125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=400993#post400993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh? What sort of concept do you have in mind, AkatsukiLeader13?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it was a concept a friend and I came up a year when talking about Exalted and stuff we'd like to do with 3E as we're the only two people in my group that backed the KS and will get backer copies. Of course its just a concept at the moment but I'd love a chance to do a test run. Though I should mention I've never actually had the chance to play Exalted. I own and have read several Exalted books, I've just never had a chance to play a game.<br /> <br /> Anyway the basic concept is that he and his twin sister (her character for the DB game I want to run with 3E) were born into one of the branches of a Great House and lived fairly typical lives for Dynast children. The two of them were close, <i>not</i> Lannister close but close. Until he had received a rather public Zenith Solar Exaltation. Needless to say, shit hit the fan for him and his family and he was forced to flee as the Wyld Hunt was literally tearing down the door of his family's estate. <br /> <br /> In the years since then he's been wandering Creation, at first seeking to prove he isn't the monster the Immaculate Order claims he is but seeing what the Realm is like beyond the Blessed Isle and the lifestyle of a Dynast he's come to realize the Realm needs to change, that it can't continue as it is and ultimately if it is to survive the Solars and Dragon-Blooded must reconcile. Of course he's been completely unaware of how much his family suffered because of him or that his sister, now a DB and extremely bitter and angry at him, has joined the Wyld Hunt specifically to hunt him down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T17:56:23-08:00","id":401133,"title":"","content":"That sounds like a pretty cool character, actually. I'd be more than willing to help you write them up, if need be, and there are several masters of the system in this game as well if you want to pose your questions to the group at large.<br /> <br /> So, it seems like we'll have two former Dynastic Scions, a demon preacher, a Lunar sage, and a robot. Or not, Magnusar hasn't shown me his proposal yet. Nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T18:05:32-08:00","id":401160,"title":"","content":"I'm not all that worried about writing up the bio, aside from names I'm good at that stuff. It will be more the character sheet I'm worried about making a mistake about but undoubtedly you'll point out any errors anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T18:08:48-08:00","id":401174,"title":"","content":"I download Anathema to create all of my exalted characters - <a href=\"http://anathema.github.io/\" target=\"_blank\">http://anathema.github.io/</a> <br /> <br /> I also use the following guide when choosing excellencies:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Also, a general run-down on excellencies.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">The 1st Excellency is great in cases where more successes=more effect, such as combat or crafting.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">The 2nd Excellency is the opposite, most useful when all you need to do is succeed.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">The 3rd Excellency is wonky, and is actually most useful for cases where you have to calculate a static value, due to the way it adds dice in.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Here's a basic rundown by ability:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Archery: 1st Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Martial Arts: 1st Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Melee: 1st Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Thrown: 1st Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">War: 2nd Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Integrity: 2nd Excellency/3rd Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Performance: 2nd Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Presence: 2nd Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Resistance: 2nd Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Survival: 2nd Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Craft: 1st Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Investigation: 2nd Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Lore: 2nd Excellency (1st Excellency if you want to Wyld Shape)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Medicine: 2nd Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Occult: 2nd Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Athletics: 3rd Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Awareness: 1st Excellency/2nd Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Dodge: 2nd Excellency/3rd Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Larceny: 2nd Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Stealth: 2nd Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Bureaucracy: 2nd Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Linguistics: 2nd Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Ride: 2nd Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Sail: 2nd Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Socialize: 2nd Excellency</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> </table></div> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T18:10:12-08:00","id":401178,"title":"","content":"Hey, AkatsukiLeader13. Which Dynast House is your character from? My character has some issues with one of the houses, so I want to make sure that isn't your house.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T18:23:02-08:00","id":401198,"title":"","content":"Haven't actually picked one yet. Like I said its at the moment just a concept that I've only just begun to flesh out for this. Of course even if they had issues with his House, short of them having a fanatical, kill them all hatred, I don't see that as a major problem.<br /> <br /> EDIT:Wonderandawe, thanks for the link. Anathema looks like it will be very helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","user":"AkatsukiLeader13","date":". 02-10-2015, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T18:28:44-08:00","id":401203,"title":"","content":"My character has been systematically trying to destroy the economic power of her husband's house for the past ten years or so. So, your character might have more issues with my character. I chose House Peleps as the house her husband is from. I considered a few other options, so I can change it if needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T18:38:39-08:00","id":401235,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. Like I said I haven't yet picked a House for him. Been getting a feel for Anathema at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T18:50:24-08:00","id":401251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=401174#post401174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also use the following guide when choosing excellencies:</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally good, but there are a few points of contention. Craft is almost always better as a second excellency because you are trying to hit a fixed number of successes and it takes some of the randomness out of the process. Larceny can also benefit from the 1st if you expect it to actually be contested in which case the chance of higher successes can be useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T19:41:23-08:00","id":401325,"title":"","content":"I would like to consider possibly throwing my hat into this one. I would most likely be building another Solar, of a different caste than the one from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\">Forging a Nation</a>. Let me sleep on it. I might just be able to convince myself that I want to do a Lunar, DB, or renegade Abyssal.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T19:55:46-08:00","id":401333,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Charms, Combos, Sorcery and all that are probably the thing I'm least sure about. As a veteran OWoD and NWoD player/ST I'm used to the Attributes, Abilities, Backgrounds and the rest so they're no problem.<br /> <br /> So I might just do the rest of the sheet and throw up what I have tomorrow for advice on Charms and stuff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T20:40:55-08:00","id":401394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=401325#post401325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to consider possibly throwing my hat into this one. I would most likely be building another Solar, of a different caste than the one from <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation&amp;quot;]Forging</a> a Nation[/URL]. Let me sleep on it. I might just be able to convince myself that I want to do a Lunar, DB, or renegade Abyssal.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be a good place to try that Abyssal you were talking about. Just a thought.<br /> <br /> Anyways, ST man- any house rules for character generation? Also, what are your thoughts on my Lunar having Wyld Artifacts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T07:23:07-08:00","id":401827,"title":"","content":"Welcome, Belkra! As Noodle said, this would be a golden chance to try out that Abyssal Cecil you mentioned before, but if you want to do other things, that'd be fine, too.<br /> <br /> @AkatsukiLeader: If you'd like help, I'm sure we can give you some assistance on charm selection. <br /> <br /> @Noodle: I prefer Schaeffer Chargen for Lunars, personally, so you can use that if you'd like. Also, I don't mind if you wanted to take gossamer artifacts if you want, although I'd like an explanation for how a Lunar got Fae magical weapons and tools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T11:34:10-08:00","id":402183,"title":"","content":"Since Exthalion asked, yes, you may use Merits and Flaws if you desire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T13:18:14-08:00","id":402319,"title":"","content":"Hey guys- we should probably establish a common language for the Circle. I'm thinking of Skytongue with either Old Realm or Riverspeak as alternates. Your thoughts?<br /> <br /> Also, does anyone playing a Solaroid want to have my Lunar as their Lunar mate? I'm open to options, though I'd prefer their relationship to be along the lines of &quot;Best Friends who are also bitter rivals&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T13:34:56-08:00","id":402339,"title":"","content":"My character can speak all three of those options. <br /> <br /> Speaking of which, here is my character sheet: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B-UiWxItb8fkem5YcU9ubzl5ZlU&amp;authuser=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B-...ZlU&amp;authuser=0</a><br /> <br /> I haven't really thought about a lunar mate for my character. Not really sure how she would react to her lunar mate either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T14:10:01-08:00","id":402412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=402319#post402319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys- we should probably establish a common language for the Circle. I'm thinking of Skytongue with either Old Realm or Riverspeak as alternates. Your thoughts?<br /> <br /> Also, does anyone playing a Solaroid want to have my Lunar as their Lunar mate? I'm open to options, though I'd prefer their relationship to be along the lines of &quot;Best Friends who are also bitter rivals&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't mind being attached to a green sun, I don't mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T14:20:58-08:00","id":402430,"title":"","content":"Ooh! A game set in the North!<br /> <br /> Dibs Haslanti Sky Captain stationed in Last Chance to defend the League's investment in developing and protecting Lastchance, who gets mixed up in adventurous nonsense. I wanna play with Haslanti dream-omens and maybe have some ties to their neato gods too.<br /> <br /> I'm leaning towards a Lunar or an Outcaste Dragonblood here.<br /> <br /> As always in Play-By-Post games, having linked backstories helps keep things moving and gets everyone past the &quot;getting to know one another&quot; stage quickly, so I'm definitely open to having one or two other PCs as friends/lovers/allies/whatever before start of game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 02-11-2015, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T14:30:01-08:00","id":402464,"title":"","content":"Wise Old Guru, I'll be interested, if you want to play a Lunar. Maybe even work with a DB background. I can send you some of my backstory to see if you are interested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T14:39:52-08:00","id":402497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=402412#post402412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't mind being attached to a green sun, I don't mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! I should be finished with my preliminary write-up shortly. I'll shoot it to you once I'm finished so we can work out how they met and such. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=402430#post402430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh! A game set in the North!<br /> <br /> Dibs Haslanti Sky Captain stationed in Last Chance to defend the League's investment in developing and protecting Lastchance, who gets mixed up in adventurous nonsense. I wanna play with Haslanti dream-omens and maybe have some ties to their neato gods too.<br /> <br /> I'm leaning towards a Lunar or an Outcaste Dragonblood here.<br /> <br /> As always in Play-By-Post games, having linked backstories helps keep things moving and gets everyone past the &quot;getting to know one another&quot; stage quickly, so I'm definitely open to having one or two other PCs as friends/lovers/allies/whatever before start of game.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you go with a Lunar, we could have the same mentor. Otherwise, I'm running with my Lunar being a Haslan as of right now. That leaves open a large number of possibilities for potentially being friends/allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T15:18:34-08:00","id":402534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=402430#post402430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh! A game set in the North!<br /> <br /> Dibs Haslanti Sky Captain stationed in Last Chance to defend the League's investment in developing and protecting Lastchance, who gets mixed up in adventurous nonsense. I wanna play with Haslanti dream-omens and maybe have some ties to their neato gods too.<br /> <br /> I'm leaning towards a Lunar or an Outcaste Dragonblood here.<br /> <br /> As always in Play-By-Post games, having linked backstories helps keep things moving and gets everyone past the &quot;getting to know one another&quot; stage quickly, so I'm definitely open to having one or two other PCs as friends/lovers/allies/whatever before start of game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome! As for the town, It's suppsoed to be Lastchance, as I originally thought that naming a place &quot;Last Chance&quot; would be asking for trouble, but I suppose it makes more sense. Last Chance it is <br /> <br /> @Noodle: Do you have anything in mind for your Lunar in terms of their mentor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T17:15:28-08:00","id":402640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=402534#post402534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Noodle: Do you have anything in mind for your Lunar in terms of their mentor?</div> </div> </div> </div>I intend for him to be a No Moon sage, though that could possibly change. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1XO7-7sbDDzHQlfAcTlJYkkM5tQR25hsKiCipa05aZdk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here's a Link</a> to my preliminary character sheet. I need to flesh out the backstory more, but it should serve to give the others a general view of my competencies and character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T17:15:39-08:00","id":402641,"title":"","content":"Also, since it seems like I've been approached by several players with almost-finished characters, I set up the OoC thread. When you're ready with your characters, if you could link them there, too, please?<br /> <br /> You can find it <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T17:43:14-08:00","id":402657,"title":"","content":"I will have the start of a character sheet done tomorrow. I am having trouble deciding what to play, though. Here are the options:<ul><li>A Lost Egg Dragonblood of Northern stock who is a consummate archer and healer</li> <li>An Abyssal Dark Knight on the road to redemption. He is very repentant about the wrongs he has committed and I expect Resonance to kick him in the feels often.</li> <li>A Solar 'Bard' who has the ability to be a womanizer but holds back on it.</li> <li>An Abyssal Necromancer who would rather destroy or banish undead than create them.</li> <li>A Dynast Dragonblood Crafter from a small house. His father left him and his four DB siblings and cousins all a hearthstone from a large Manse that was altered to create multiple hearthstones. Some have already hinted that they have no problem with shedding blood to increase their stake in the Manse.</li> <li>No Moon Lupine Lunar. (Do I really need to say more here?)</li> </ul><br /> I think I will stop there. That's quite a few choices already. Note: I really love paladins, wolves, and Gothic stuff. Paladins are my favorite archetype, but Necromancers come second. If I can combine wolves and paladins, yeah...I'd be in heaven.<br /> <br /> I will take suggestions, but I don't want you guys to think this is a vote. Even if all of you pick one and I just decide I'm not feeling it, please don't get upset if I don't go with it. I'm excited about this. I love the North. Bring on the snow and ice!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T18:25:33-08:00","id":402702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=402657#post402657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will have the start of a character sheet done tomorrow. I am having trouble deciding what to play, though. Here are the options:<ul><li>A Lost Egg Dragonblood of Northern stock who is a consummate archer and healer</li> <li>An Abyssal Dark Knight on the road to redemption. He is very repentant about the wrongs he has committed and I expect Resonance to kick him in the feels often.</li> <li>A Solar 'Bard' who has the ability to be a womanizer but holds back on it.</li> <li>An Abyssal Necromancer who would rather destroy or banish undead than create them.</li> <li>A Dynast Dragonblood Crafter from a small house. His father left him and his four DB siblings and cousins all a hearthstone from a large Manse that was altered to create multiple hearthstones. Some have already hinted that they have no problem with shedding blood to increase their stake in the Manse.</li> <li>No Moon Lupine Lunar. (Do I really need to say more here?)</li> </ul><br /> I think I will stop there. That's quite a few choices already. Note: I really love paladins, wolves, and Gothic stuff. Paladins are my favorite archetype, but Necromancers come second. If I can combine wolves and paladins, yeah...I'd be in heaven.<br /> <br /> I will take suggestions, but I don't want you guys to think this is a vote. Even if all of you pick one and I just decide I'm not feeling it, please don't get upset if I don't go with it. I'm excited about this. I love the North. Bring on the snow and ice!</div> </div> </div> </div>Those seem familiar. Wait a second, is that the cast of FF4? Anna, Cecil, Edward, Rydia, Cid, and Kain? Or am I off-base here?<br /> <br /> That being said, you can easily combine the wolves and paladins. The Haslan have a strong affinity for animal gods, and one of the Icewalker tribes I was going to have a few NPCs be from are the Weiss Zahne, a cannibalistic clan of nomads under the protection of the goddess of Polestar Wolves, giant horse-sized wolves so used to life in the North that they have ice in their blood. So, between being a devotee of a wolf god, being a beastman, or even being a Lupine Lunar devoted to protecting Creation? That sounds pretty paladin-like to me.<br /> <br /> Hell, let's go one step further, and add in Necromancy. You have your Lupine Lunar No Moon. Have them utilize Necromancy as a means to kill the undead, and protect their loved ones from the Wyld and the zombie hordes of the Bishop and the Lover.<br /> <br /> This gets to another thing, I'm not a fan of Lunars being gimped in terms of Necromancy. No Moons are supposed to be preeminent occultists, and yet they can barely scratch the surface of it. Bollocks to that, I say. Lunars get access to the Labyrinth Circle as well. <br /> <br /> I hope that helps, although all of those concepts are good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T18:38:28-08:00","id":402736,"title":"","content":"The first Dragonblood is loosely based on Rosa Farrell from FFIV, and the Dark Knight is definitely a Cecil Harvey wannabe. The others are just things that I have wanted to play for a while either in other games (including my favorite online game) or Exalted. I definitely didn't rip FFIV that much regardless of how big a fanboy I am.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T05:59:53-08:00","id":403227,"title":"","content":"Hm. Okay, I'm leaning Lunar. They fit in well with secret powers within and behind the Haslanit, and plus the North is full of situations where shapeshifting is really handy.<br /> <br /> So, the question becomes...<br /> <br /> Do I play the Leopard Seal Lunar I've wanted to play for ages, or the Osprey Lunar I've wanted to play since Forumquest went with the badger?<br /> <br /> This Emerald have any major lakes or streams?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T06:15:28-08:00","id":403236,"title":"","content":"I'd admit I have a soft spot for Bird of Prey shape shifters due to my favorite childhood book series, Animorphs. But if you have been wanting to play a seal for ages, then do it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Here is some background on my character for the rest of the party:<br /> <br /> Zarah has been in the north for about a month or two. She is fresh from the Blessed Isle and it shows. She has no basic survival skills, but has managed to thrive by using what little money she has to make some good investment choices in the area. She is still trying to get use to the more informal Northern methods of law, contracts, and ownership. Fortunately, she is a quick study.<br /> <br /> Zarah doesn't really stand out, unlike most social characters. She is there in the background, making deals and getting things done. People who have had business dealings with her know her to be reliable and willing to bend a few rules to see results. She is basically that person at work that everyone knows but no one thinks about until they need something done right. Though, in the North, she doesn't have many contacts as she did on the Blessed Isle.<br /> <br /> Also, she is not above breaking a few laws to see results. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I will be away from internet access for the next few days. I'll be back on Sunday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-12-2015, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T07:37:51-08:00","id":403309,"title":"","content":"Here is Twenty-Fifth Merciful, Pyrian Malefactor.<br /> <br /> Sheet<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FikCyri95Tod9dXWTHNVcOZuh1JsS6JkHoFRvMm9Uyo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Backstory<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Once there was a Mortal\u2026<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Once there was a man of Whitewall who lived his life. That he did this may seem trivial, but he did not think so then. This man was a mine foreman, like his father and grandfather before him. Times were sometimes lean, but there was always food, clothing, and shelter. The family had heat in winter and enough leisure that their spirits were not ground down.<br /> <br /> Eventually, only slightly younger than was expected, this man was married. Her name was Elenore, and she was a smiling young woman he thought beautiful. Their first child, a healthy boy, was born not long after. The child was the light of their lives so they named him Aiden. Six years later a daughter joined the family in the spring. The day she was born there was a rainbow around the sun so they called her Enfys because she had brought new color to their lives.<br /> <br /> For many years the man of Whitewall was content. When it pleased Heaven there were difficult times or easy but the man was wise enough to know the same was true for everyone. Whatever he did later, it was a decent life and he knew it.<br /> <br /> Some years ago his father was killed when a tunnel collapsed. For years the output of the mine had been dwindling and so the owners had directed the foremen to dig new and more numerous tunnels in the hopes of uncovering additional seams so that they could fulfill their own obligations. As the most experienced under-foreman, the man replaced his father as overseer of the mine. Though the owners sympathized they continued to require new delving. So the man of Whitewall did his job and met every quota even as the number of accident continued to increase.<br /> <br /> Around this time his wife became pregnant with their third child. In the midst of moving to the overseer\u2019s quarters that his father had previously occupied the man evaluated his life and began to grow dissatisfied. He foresaw his son following in his profession, as he had followed in his father\u2019s; he foresaw his daughter marrying the son of one of his workmen, as his wife had done; and he foresaw himself dying in the house he was born in, if he were lucky. It wasn\u2019t good enough. His children deserved a better life than he had lived.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> \u2026who became a Mendicant.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">From time to time a miner or ruin delver would find some treasure and bring it to the city. Even the least of these was worth enough to buy a life richer than the man of Whitewall led. So he began to spend less time with his family, even though they needed him more, and searched the caves and clefs near the mine he oversaw for the thing that would bring comfort to his wife and security to his children.<br /> <br /> It was in one such cave, while sheltering from a sudden storm, that he thought he found what he thought he was looking for. The room he found himself in was a large, vaulted hall and everything seemed to shine with gold and amber light. It was like none of the ruins his workers occasionally discovered and nothing resembled the objects he expected to find. He disregarded the uncertainty of unfamiliarity and continued deeper into the hall. At the far end was a stone pyre and on that a sword that could not be mistaken for mundane. He wrapped it in his cloak and departed for the city at once. The storm that forced him into the cave had subsided with every step he took across the hall.<br /> <br /> When he stepped into Whitewall the blade freed itself from his grip and the cloak it was wrapped in settled as though some unseen person wore it. The raksha whose sword grace he had taken into the city laughed as it began to slay whatever its gaze fell upon whether that thing was male or female, child or adult, human or beast. No blood ran through the streets, each stroke painted an epitaph on the white walls describing the beauty of every death. In that fashion the fey ran through the streets, singing as it went. The man never discovered how or if it was stopped.<br /> <br /> No one came to visit him during the several months he was in prison afterwards. If they were not permitted to come or never tried to he chooses not to know.<br /> <br /> When the time for the yearly sacrifice came he and everyone else guilty of high crimes were gathered and the guards began to read from the list given to them. Some of those they called were dead, hoping to avoid this fate. Yet one by one twenty-three were chosen. His was the last name called. They shackled him, unresisting, to the rest of the grim-faced chosen. As they did so, a man was dragged screaming into the room. This man, whose name had been called already, had escaped the week before and just been recaptured. Mutely, the man of Whitewall watched as his bonds were removed and affixed to the struggling man.<br /> <br /> Both guards and prisoners muttered about Twenty-Fifth Merciful as they returned to their duties and cells. As he too went back he caught the attention of his guard and asked what they were talking about. \u201cThey are talking of the god who whispers in the judges\u2019 ears as they pen the fatal lists, who led the hunters as they tracked that man, and who has seen fit to save you just now though you offered him nothing. It seems he does not care that you failed to pray, for they will pray again come next year. They always do.\u201d<br /> <br /> The next night, glad in prison rags, he too was thrown beyond the gate though no unseelie host or restless dead waited. Some of the other exiles were met by friends or family who provided them with food or warm clothing, most were not. He walked for a while, he didn\u2019t notice toward which direction, until his strength gave out in the cold.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He confronted his Mortality...<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The man of Whitewall watched the sky for a time, his frostbitten limbs lay still when he tried to move them. The only sound was the whisper of the stars as his breath froze and fell. Then the ringing became a wordless voice and began to speak to him.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is fitting that you die here, abandon and broken; the whole world is dying.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was silence while he drew another pained breath. He thought he had gone made, and found he didn\u2019t care. \u201cI tried, suffered, so they wouldn\u2019t have to...\u201d As he finished the tinkling began again.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is fitting that your own actions damn you; the whole world is damned.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey should have better...\u201d The pain of cold began to retreat, replaced by a warmth he knew meant his limbs were dying.<br /> <br /> \u201cYour kind was never meant for this, never meant to rule or rise above your station.<br /> So here you, as the world, die. It is time to try another way.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cToo late now, too tired and too weak\u2026\u201d The warmth had faded too, now there was no feeling at all.<br /> <br /> \u201cLet go of your liberty. Lay down your rights. Surrender everything to the hands that made you.<br /> Be reconciled to them and to the rightness you have never known.\u201d<br /> <br /> The man from Whitewall didn\u2019t have enough strength to draw another breath. As he finished that last exhalation his black lips formed the shape of a single word.<br /> <br /> It was enough.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ... and met a Malefactor...<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">He sought Company in Misery...<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It was night again when the man of Whitewall next awoke. Fragments of smoking ice surrounded him and the air was freezing air was pleasant. He looked down at himself without recognition. The charcoal grey of frostbite still stained his skin and his flesh was cold to the touch. After a few moments he gave up the examination. What he looked like didn\u2019t matter and besides, it was fitting.<br /> <br /> The first person he met was one of those prisoners who had received aid. Now she lay dying as he had been and no demon waited for her.<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you want to live?\u201d he said as her eyes opened wide in recognition.<br /> <br /> \u201cPlease\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWill you accept the pain that life brings?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes.\u201d Her answer was the same as his had been. Her fate should be no different.<br /> <br /> \u201cFor the life you have lost and the life you have been given, you owe me two services. You shall carry them out all the days of your life or a harsher and more binding doom will come upon you. First, seven times each day you will offer me prayer of thanksgiving. Fail in this and I command you go to Marama\u2019s Fell and cry out that you wish your soul beaten into iron until the hungry dead come for you. Second, you will see to comfort of the widow of the miner who was exiled with you, so long as your aid is never known. Shirk this duty and I command you seek out the Winter Court and proclaim you come that they might make you sad forever. Do you understand me exile?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, Twenty-Fifth Merciful. Forgive me, for I did not believe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYour belief is not required, only your obedience.\u201d Those were the last words he spoke to her as he walked away.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ... and found it in a Broken City.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Not every stranger in the wastes was commanded to see to the comfort of a family in Whitewall. The North is too vast for such an order to be meaningful. Still, Haslanti scouts, lost Guildsmen, and Icewalker not-yet-men accepted his offer just as readily as anyone else. Nor was it only humans who fell into his debt. Eventually, the petty victories no longer satisfied him. Those who fell into his power were individuals, their lives and failings were small. He was made to break kingdoms. So be started to call in favors.<br /> <br /> At a site south of Icehome, Guild thaumaturges began to summon demons en mass. Some were seized at once by their fellows to be rendered into calcanth while others began to clear the space. Using techniques forgotten when the Lintha, fell demonic artisans shaped their kin into buildings, roads, plazas, and other architectural features. When the trap was finished he called human debtors to him and dispatched them to report the discovery of the \u201cruin of the Age of Splendors\u201d.<br /> <br /> The powers of the area began to converge on the icy ruin. At first their scouting parties maintained an uneasy peace. Then they began to die. They quickly cast blame on each other and soon the Agata streets shone red in the Gilmyne light. The nations sent angry messages back and forth, until head began to cool and talk of peace and reparations began. That was when the second wave of favors came due and previously moderate parties began to agitate. The killing stroke came when the sorcerer of the Haslanti responsible for Infallible Messages fell into Twenty-Fifth Merciful\u2019s power. Where once it seemed war might be averted, hostilities began with surprising fervor.<br /> <br /> Calling more and yet more favors due, Merciful caused the conflict to escalate further. Atrocity was answered with atrocity until no less than three of the irreplaceable greenfields were reduced to ash. Only then did the belligerents realize the scope of what they had done. When a full accounting of death and damage was taken the totals were staggering. The intervention of the Bull of the North and the Realm had left everyone weakened and exposed. Five nations and three greenfields had been involved and so what had started as an Exalted\u2019s dissatisfaction was called the War of Five Kings and Three Valleys.<br /> <br /> The ruin that followed was pleasing to the Ebon Dragon.</div></div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> yet he is still a Man.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Twenty-Fifth Merciful remembers the name his parents gave him, but he makes no use of it. Better that he died in Winter Exile than knowledge of what he became stain his family\u2019s reputation further. It is for that same reason that those of his cult near the city live in such fear of allowing their assistance to be known.<br /> <br /> Though he has ruined thousands of lives in service to the Yozi, the urge Adorjan placed on his soul has never grown less keen. The discomfort it brings him is visible in his eyes, everyone he looks upon seems to hide some foulness that must be exposed. Yet for all that other people are unlovely to him, he finds himself most abhorrent. Even with all that he has done for his new masters, very little has really changed. He knows that his own pettiness, the longing to ensure three, or perhaps four, mortals are taken care of, holds him back from his duty.<br /> <br /> It may be petty, but he still wants to smile as Aiden begged to come to work with him or see Enfys dancing in the springtime or watch Elenore sing by the riverside.<br /> <br /> When he thinks of them he cannot see the flaw that he has been commanded to exploit. He knows his wife and children, knows they are imperfect, and knows that none of them deserve what he does to those who\u2019s wishes he grants. This realization has made him wonder how much of the ruin that he has unleashed occurred not because of the weakness of his victims, but because he pushed men and women farther than they would ever have gone on their own.</div></div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Note: There is no god actually called Twenty-Fifth Merciful. The god's theoretical purview belongs to the Syndics. However, humans are irrational creatures and prisoners and family are desperate to believe that something can be done. And where there are desperate people there are cons willing to tell them what they want to hear (and cash in). So people invent new rituals every year and families pay disreputable thaumaturges, and the ones who live believe that what they did had something to do with it.<br /> <br /> Also, there is a backstory section I haven't written, and may not get around to what with RL, about him dealing with the guilt of his actions by going to Malfeas, meeting the Pyrian Flame, and achieving a math-zen when he entered her name where she dwells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T16:42:25-08:00","id":403847,"title":"","content":"Okay. Leopard Seal Lunar is a go. <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/sgyy6wiu59rmohe/Nergui.docx?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Here's a link to my character sheet. It's just a big ol' word document. </a><br /> <br /> I've taken Keen-Eyed Snowcat as a Lunar Mentor, since she's affiliated with the Haslanti League and their intelligence services, but if you have another Mentor in mind (possibly one that Nergui and another Lunar PC can share), I'm fine changing that.<br /> <br /> Nergui does have an airship and a crew of three NPC followers, one of whom is a scout with a Haslanti glider. The airship has room for seven passengers in addition to the crew, so if the party needs a ride, a ride they shall have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T18:01:30-08:00","id":403939,"title":"","content":"@Belkra: Ah, okay. Well, I hope that helps.<br /> <br /> @Wonderandawe: That's fine. I hope you have a good time, then!<br /> <br /> @Exthalion: You adjusted him a bit, I see, since I saw him last. <br /> <br /> That's quite a character, there, Old Wise Guru. I quite like him. I guess an explanation is in order for the question before of the existence of rivers or lakes in the Emerald. There are in fact, several lakes and even a system of rivers. They exist nearby where Last Chance exists, bubbling up from an alabaster marble structure that the the natives of Last Chance have dubbed the Eternal Ice Tower for how the chilly, pure water seems to endlessly flow from it. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T18:03:29-08:00","id":403940,"title":"","content":"Alright, I'm going with the Necromancer. I should have a sheet ready to post sometime this weekend. I'm thinking of having him be a thaumaturge ghost hunter that got on the wrong side of the Deathlord that exalted him. The character will be of the opinion that the Deathlord was a fool for giving him even more of an ability to destroy undead, even the Deathlords themselves if he wanted to. Of course, the Deathlord could just be toying with him and letting him think he has that ability now.<br /> <br /> Okay, so I want to have Necromancy out of the gate. I am going to assume that is allowed. I would also like suggestions for some beginning spells. I also think I will be taking Thaumaturgy, a remnant of what the character had in life, unless that isn't allowed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T18:13:54-08:00","id":403948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=403939#post403939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Exthalion: You adjusted him a bit, I see, since I saw him last.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't sure how to allocate Enemy and Secret. The Secret bothers him more because if it got out, and something happened to them, there will be dead people.<br /> <br /> If you meant Known-Anathema + the Ebon Dragon disguise charms (I swear that just occurred to me) I can reduce it to the Lunar level.<br /> <br /> Was there anything else?<br /> <br /> Also, is the Urge too on the nose?<br /> <br /> Edit: The trip to Malfeas might explain the Ebon Dragon Charms as part of the character and relation to SHLiHN better. I will get writing on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 02-12-2015, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T18:28:31-08:00","id":403959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=403940#post403940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I'm going with the Necromancer. I should have a sheet ready to post sometime this weekend. I'm thinking of having him be a thaumaturge ghost hunter that got on the wrong side of the Deathlord that exalted him. The character will be of the opinion that the Deathlord was a fool for giving him even more of an ability to destroy undead, even the Deathlords themselves if he wanted to. Of course, the Deathlord could just be toying with him and letting him think he has that ability now.<br /> <br /> Okay, so I want to have Necromancy out of the gate. I am going to assume that is allowed. I would also like suggestions for some beginning spells. I also think I will be taking Thaumaturgy, a remnant of what the character had in life, unless that isn't allowed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thaumaturgy is allowed, by all means. As per Necromancy I've found, through NPCs, that anything that creates war machines is pretty rad. Also, spells like Flesh Sloughing Wave SOUND cool on paper, but when you begin chanting in battle, most everyone tends to stop what they're doing and hurl rocks at you until you botch, and then you're left with a front half that is lacking all that meat you're used to. <br /> <br /> My question would be, who is his Deathlord? There's the Bishop to the West and the Lover to the East, and another, the Glacial Tyrant of Unfettered Disaster, to the south. The Tyrant is homebrew, though, FYI. <br /> <br /> @Exthalion: Yeah, those were what immediately stuck out to me. Not bad points, just something I noticed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T01:17:05-08:00","id":404240,"title":"","content":"Are you guys still recruiting for this game? If so, I wouldn't mind throwing my hat into the race. I have a concept dancing around in my head of a Dawn Caste 'monster hunter' who slays the greatest beasts of Creation for sport. (This concept could also work for a Full Moon Lunar, but a quick skim tells me we already have a Lunar). And if that doesn't work, I literally have a gazillion other ideas for a character in the north.<br /> <br /> If there's no more room though, I'll be on my way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":814,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","user":"dreamking89","date":". 02-13-2015, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T02:50:15-08:00","id":404340,"title":"","content":"Wise Old Guru, if your character is looking for &quot;someone to know&quot; I had an idea.<br /> <br /> I'm now considering a Dawn Caste sky pirate/thief/scoundrel who the Haslanti aren't exactly fond of. It might be fun to make them a Solar/Lunar pairing and have Nergui recently have captured my character.<br /> <br /> Just a thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T09:05:23-08:00","id":404525,"title":"","content":"Welcome, Dreamking89! We still have room. A Dawn Caste would probably put Wonderandawe at ease, considering how their character only dipped their toe into combat abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T14:30:33-08:00","id":405107,"title":"","content":"I'd like to join, playing a Terrestrial Immaculate Priestess who's recently realized her entire religion is a damn hoax and is currently traveling with the group. Not sure which charms I'd use, she'd be the first terrestrial I'd actually build myself, and I'm open to suggestions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T16:30:34-08:00","id":405256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=405107#post405107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to join, playing a Terrestrial Immaculate Priestess who's recently realized her entire religion is a damn hoax and is currently traveling with the group. Not sure which charms I'd use, she'd be the first terrestrial I'd actually build myself, and I'm open to suggestions.</div> </div> </div> </div>They'd work well with the Solar character I'm building. He was born into Dynast family only become a Zenith as a teenager, forcing him to go on the run. In the years he's become a wandering hero/revolutionary preacher, who despite it all is actually loyal to the Realm but at the same time has come to see the corruption and decadence of the Realm and wants nothing more than to see it corrected. Chief among that is a reconciliation between the Solars and the Dragon-Blooded. Of course as long as the half-truths and lies of the Immaculate Order are being supported he knows that can't happen so he's working on his own revisions to the Immaculate Philosophy, creating a few scattered cults across the North in an effort to spread his beliefs amid the people of Threshold before eventually returning to the Blessed Isle to spread them within the heart of the Realm itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T17:50:34-08:00","id":406201,"title":"","content":"Welcome, Revenge of the TV Head. Do you have any ideas on your priestess' aspect or martial art, if any, she has focused on for her enlightenment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T19:22:16-08:00","id":406249,"title":"","content":"Okay so I've finished <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B9whWahX5jabWWptYkNUUzlMSEE/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">my character sheet</a>, minus the Charms and bonus points. And like I said earlier I'm not quite sure which Charms I should go for. Like I said above, he's a wandering hero and preacher, protecting the helpless while spreading his revised interpretation of the Immaculate Philosophy.<br /> <br /> I have a bit of an idea on what I'm going for with the bonus points, though advice on that is welcome too.<br /> <br /> Oh, and double checking the sheet I realized that I didn't specify the Artifact he has, its a Grand Grimscythe. Was very tempted to go with the Grand Daiklave but I've always had a thing for scythes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T19:34:08-08:00","id":406274,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was definitely thinking of taking Shadowlands Circle Necromancy. Spells would include Banish Ghost, Iron Countermagic, and Gentle Call of Lethe. I would also have the Art of the Dead at a high degree. Yes these are pretty redundant, but I believe there will be times when one or the other is preferable. Also, since he was a Thaumaturge before receiving the Black Exaltation, he would retain those abilities despite having more efficient and powerful ones now.<br /> <br /> I would like to have his primary armament be a staff (I will have to try to find an artifact version as these aren't available in core) for when the crap hits the fan. I will most likely dip into Melee to represent his nod to wanting to not be completely useless when blades are bared. I know a staff has the Martial Arts tag, but that would represent a conscious decision to be a combatant and I don't think that is his style...yet. The thing is Abysals (like Solars) sword so freakin' hard. I just can't ignore that. I'm also thinking I would do some thrown in order to stand apart from combat, but I will have to approach that at a different time. Of course, if I wanted to depict a fall into darkness I could branch into MA and pull out a combination of Savage Shade and Dark Messiah. Hmm...<br /> <br /> I will tell you what I am having trouble deciding: Darklord choice and actual freakin' name for the character. What should I name him? Suggestions are welcome. I would like to know more about the Tyrant before I actually make a decision on that ground. Other than that and being freakin' busy for the past two or three days, the character is coming along nicely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T19:47:02-08:00","id":406302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=406249#post406249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so I've finished <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B9whWahX5jabWWptYkNUUzlMSEE/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">my character sheet</a>, minus the Charms and bonus points. And like I said earlier I'm not quite sure which Charms I should go for. Like I said above, he's a wandering hero and preacher, protecting the helpless while spreading his revised interpretation of the Immaculate Philosophy.<br /> <br /> I have a bit of an idea on what I'm going for with the bonus points, though advice on that is welcome too.<br /> <br /> Oh, and double checking the sheet I realized that I didn't specify the Artifact he has, its a Grand Grimscythe. Was very tempted to go with the Grand Daiklave but I've always had a thing for scythes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will it be a problem that I am a priest of the Yozi whose urge is to cultivate the character flaws in people that lead them to ruin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T20:43:53-08:00","id":406319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=406302#post406302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Will it be a problem that I am a priest of the Yozi whose urge is to cultivate the character flaws in people that lead them to ruin?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exthalion how are we supposed to get along with your character when his motivation is somewhat to brainwash us into self-destruction ? This is by no mean an insult but just a bit of concern since I play an alchemical it might be a bit tense with the primordial and Yozis patronage.<br /> <br /> Here is my character: Unrestrained Lover of Technological Advancement<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Unrestrained Lover of Technological Advancement<br /> Concept: Weapon Scientist<br /> Caste: Orichalcum<br /> Anima Banner: Yellow lightning crack aroud him while gears and others bits of machinery form a terrible war automaton bristling with weapons it's head is a human skull with mechanical eyes.<br /> Motivation: Find or Create a technology to eradicate the void from the great maker<br /> <br /> Caste Attributes<br /> Strenght: 3<br /> Charisma: 3<br /> Intelligence: 5 (6)<br /> <br /> Favored Attributes<br /> Dexterity: 3<br /> Stamina: 2<br /> Wits: 5<br /> <br /> Other Attributes<br /> Appearance: 2<br /> Perception: 3<br /> Manipulation: 2<br /> <br /> Warfare<br /> Archery: 3 + 1 Essence Weapons<br /> Athletics:<br /> Awerenes:<br /> Dodge:<br /> Integrity: 3<br /> Martial Arts:<br /> Melee:<br /> Resistance:<br /> Thrown:<br /> War:<br /> <br /> Labor<br /> Craft: 4<br /> Larceny:<br /> Linguistics: 2 (Native: Autochtonian, Old Realm, Skytongue)<br /> Performance:<br /> Presence:<br /> Ride:<br /> Sail:<br /> Socialise:<br /> Stealth:<br /> Survival:<br /> <br /> Learning<br /> Bureaucracy:<br /> Investigation:<br /> Lore: 5 +2 Magitech Weapons<br /> Medicine:<br /> Occult: 5<br /> <br /> Charms (4 General slot, 5 Dedicated slot)<br /> Strenght<br /> -<br /> Charisma<br /> -<br /> Intelligence<br /> - First Intelligence Augmentation (1m) (1m per die added)<br /> - Fourth Intelligence Augmentation (1m)<br /> - Sixth Intelligence Augmentation (Craft) (1m)<br /> - Omnitool implant (1m) (4m activation)<br /> Dexterity<br /> - First Dexterity Augmentation (1m)<br /> - Dynamic Reaction Enhancement System (144) (1m) (2m cost to activate)<br /> - Transhuman Efficiency Relays (1m)<br /> Wits<br /> - Incomparable Efficiency Upgrade (144) (6m,1w cost to activate)<br /> - Transcendent Multimodal Artifact Matrix (168) (1m)<br /> - Essence pulse cannon (Cost one mote per shot/Cost 5m to deploy)<br /> Speed 6, Accuracy +2, Damage 10L/15B, Rate 3, Range 100, Tags F, P<br /> Stamina<br /> -<br /> Backgrounds 7/10<br /> - Artifacts 4<br /> - Precision Goggles (Artifact 2)<br /> - Flaw scanner (Artifact 1)<br /> - Transformative clothing (Artifact 1)<br /> -<br /> - Savant 3<br /> - Backing 3 Jadeborn<br /> -<br /> <br /> Essence: 3<br /> Personnal: 17<br /> Peripheral: 43/51 (8 commited)<br /> <br /> Willpower: 10<br /> compassion: 2 Temperance: 2<br /> Conviction: 3 Valor: 2<br /> <br /> Soak: 1L/2B<br /> <br /> Health:<br /> <br /> Clarity 0/10<br /> <br /> Bonus points 19/20<br /> - 10 Raise essence from 2 to 3.<br /> - 5 raise willpower from 5 to 10.<br /> - 3 points to buy 1 dedicated charm slot<br /> - 1 point to buy one charm<br /> <br /> <br /> Merits and flaws<br /> - Obligation 2pts The Beast as said that it would be back to request his help one day.<br /> <br /> Background<br /> Commissioned five years ago by the city of Arat to work in the munifactory as a artificer and researcher though he aquited himself quite well he was never fully satified with is work. It was never enough for him and the other alchemicals started to grow tired of his attitude but his results where good and so they endured it but it was not to last. An incident occured in one of the lab that was working with elsewhere technologies which triggered a massive but concentrated blast of essence that desintegrated most of what was in it's path but not Unrestrained Lover who was caught in it. Of the alchemical no trace remained behind but death did not claimed him for he found himself in a strange of cold and snow with terrible winds carriying ice that cut like glass. Confused, lost and freezing he began to wander to find shelter but instead was found by a strange beast that walked and talked like a man, the beast did not introduced itself nor did he said who sent only that he was here to guide him to safety and help understand where he was.<br /> <br /> The beast though clearly surprised by the alchemical nature of Unrestrained Lover guided him to a herd of mammoth to get some supplies for the alchemical and hunted one of the herd for it's skin an meat to continue on their journey. The beast explained where the alchemical was and it was not long before Unrestrained Lover got one thing for sure he was no longer in Autochtonia.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I want to throw him with the Hastlani League as a magitech engineer do you still have a spot on your airship for a passenger Wise Old Guru ? I might need a ride.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 02-15-2015, 12:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T21:36:25-08:00","id":406339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=406319#post406319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exthalion how are we supposed to get along with your character when his motivation is somewhat to brainwash us into self-destruction ? This is by no mean an insult but just a bit of concern since I play an alchemical it might be a bit tense with the primordial and Yozis patronage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entirely OOC: His motivation is to ensure his wife and children live long and happy lives. Since he is too ashamed to interact with them directly and is fairly sure that doing so would put them at risk he seeks that goal by making the age better for everyone.<br /> <br /> His Urge of cultivating character flaws is what the Ebon Dragon put on top of his to-do list. It can be worked out on our enemies and generally bad people. He personally hopes that people will resist him in this; that rather than give in to their flaws they will overcome them. (He does have a rather low opinion of those who do give in though, partly because that is what he did)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T23:41:01-08:00","id":406415,"title":"","content":"I am glad to hear we've got some water and rivers in the area. Gives Nergui a chance to shine.<br /> <br /> In terms of getting PCs together...if we have several PCs traveling to Last Chance from the South, it makes sense that the <i>Dancing Pelican</i> is the ship that carries you from one of the other Haslanti cities up to the emerald that's the site of the game. The ship has room for a couple of passengers in addition to the crew. In terms of Lunar/Solar mates, I'm trying to decide between picking the mate who will cause the most dramatic emotional damage and interpersonal complications, or the mate who can act as a healing and stabilizing influence for an already-unstable PC.<br /> <br /> I'll think on that.<br /> <br /> Magnusaur, you're looking to play an Alchemical fish-out-of-water? Assuming he's okayed, without access to your homeworld and the vats, how are you planning to to switch out charms or get new ones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T01:30:22-08:00","id":406502,"title":"","content":"I'm still debating my character backstory/concept/etc. Unfortunately, the North is one of the areas of Creation I know the least about, which makes it a bit hard to build a character (for me anyway)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T06:32:35-08:00","id":406635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=406415#post406415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Magnusaur, you're looking to play an Alchemical fish-out-of-water? Assuming he's okayed, without access to your homeworld and the vats, how are you planning to to switch out charms or get new ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the exact words Dietaku answered me when I asked about that in a PM.<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Dietaku: We can handle it the same way Modern does. Whenever you want to alter your charm layouts or raise your essence, your body goes dormant and the exaltation rebuilds itself in a new and stronger form/ altered magical circuit layout in the case of charms. If anyone asks, , it could be an alteration caused by the Elsewhere accident that your character went through.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> I focused my character on a crafting because he arrived to creation with the clothes on his back and he was working in a laboratory. If you want to have a magitech engineer on your ship in case it breaks down or arm it I'm your guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T07:51:09-08:00","id":406698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dreamking89</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=406502#post406502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still debating my character backstory/concept/etc. Unfortunately, the North is one of the areas of Creation I know the least about, which makes it a bit hard to build a character (for me anyway)</div> </div> </div> </div>You can always do what I did for my Northern Skype game, build a character with a backstory in an area you do know a lot about and have them run away to the North. The ST made it so that my character's First Age incarnation was based in the North, thus why my character felt drawn there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T08:00:51-08:00","id":406703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=406201#post406201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Welcome, Revenge of the TV Head. Do you have any ideas on your priestess' aspect or martial art, if any, she has focused on for her enlightenment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just that she's an Air Aspect, I've got her ability spread picked out. I'm also working with Anathema, and have no idea what I'm doing, for some reason whenever I start picking up charms, it uses the bonus points instead of the 5 charms listed under &quot;General.&quot; Which stymies me because I can only buy like, three charms with those points.<br /> <br /> Only exception seems to be when I take &quot;Pasiap's Humility.&quot; That uses up one of five charm pieces. Also, it seems as if I've forgotten to select her attributes. Heh..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T08:17:34-08:00","id":406725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=406302#post406302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will it be a problem that I am a priest of the Yozi whose urge is to cultivate the character flaws in people that lead them to ruin?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on things. I doubt many of our characters will actually know each other at the start, we're a bit too diverse of a group to just be together without some backstory. Likely we'll start off as individuals and/or smaller groups that arrive at this place with roughly similar goals, joining together to achieve said goals.<br /> <br /> Plus aside from Solars and DBs my character is pretty ignorant on the other Exalted out there. He's heard stories but never actually met any of the other types yet and his own experience with truth and the teachings of the Immaculate Order have taught him that the words of others isn't necessarily the truth. He doesn't ignore them but he doesn't accept the tales as truth either. When meeting another Exalted for the first time, he approaches them with caution until he feels he has figured out their true nature. Unless your character acts like a monster or a cruel tyrant he will tolerate them.<br /> <br /> Which given your own words...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=406339#post406339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Entirely OOC: His motivation is to ensure his wife and children live long and happy lives. Since he is too ashamed to interact with them directly and is fairly sure that doing so would put them at risk he seeks that goal by making the age better for everyone.<br /> <br /> His Urge of cultivating character flaws is what the Ebon Dragon put on top of his to-do list. It can be worked out on our enemies and generally bad people. He personally hopes that people will resist him in this; that rather than give in to their flaws they will overcome them. (He does have a rather low opinion of those who do give in though, partly because that is what he did)</div> </div> </div> </div>It shouldn't be a problem right off the bat.<br /> <br /> Don't the road though, who's to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T17:59:02-08:00","id":407199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=406698#post406698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can always do what I did for my Northern Skype game, build a character with a backstory in an area you do know a lot about and have them run away to the North. The ST made it so that my character's First Age incarnation was based in the North, thus why my character felt drawn there.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually broke my character creation block. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T18:38:12-08:00","id":407215,"title":"","content":"Question: You need a mentor to have Martial Arts Charms, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T18:43:17-08:00","id":407217,"title":"","content":"Yes, except for Hero styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T18:47:34-08:00","id":407218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dreamking89</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=407215#post407215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: You need a mentor to have Martial Arts Charms, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. It does provide a trainer for learning new ones if they know the style. This cuts down on training times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T18:50:17-08:00","id":407220,"title":"","content":"Hmm.... I thought you did need a mentor. I guess that it depends on the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T19:17:39-08:00","id":407254,"title":"","content":"I'll wait for Dietaku's final word,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T19:19:45-08:00","id":407255,"title":"","content":"I'm leaning toward selecting the Bishop as the Deathlord. It is said that he rarely selects those that don't already believe in the Shining Path, but since this character would be so staunchly against it, it would prove the validity of the religion if one so opposed could be brought to heel by the Bishop. The sheer amount of story material generated by a renegade Deathknight trying to keep from being brainwashed by the Bishop, while trying to destroy him and his servants is very appealing to me. His odds of success are very limited. He expects to die in the effort, and should he succeed, he has The Lover and another eleven Deathlords to worry about.<br /> <br /> I am picturing this Abyssal as being very much more intellectually inclined than the Dawn I am playing in Forging a Nation. Sure, that guy is smart, but there is a difference between being smart and being intellectual. He may very well learn that he needs to be more socially inclined to survive on the path he has chosen, but that remains to be seen. The trouble would be convincing him of that fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T19:22:52-08:00","id":407258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=407255#post407255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm leaning toward selecting the Bishop as the Deathlord. It is said that he rarely selects those that don't already believe in the Shining Path, but since this character would be so staunchly against it, it would prove the validity of the religion if one so opposed could be brought to heel by the Bishop. The sheer amount of story material generated by a renegade Deathknight trying to keep from being brainwashed by the Bishop, while trying to destroy him and his servants is very appealing to me. His odds of success are very limited. He expects to die in the effort, and should he succeed, he has The Lover and another eleven Deathlords to worry about.<br /> <br /> I am picturing this Abyssal as being very much more intellectually inclined than the Dawn I am playing in Forging a Nation. Sure, that guy is smart, but there is a difference between being smart and being intellectual. He may very well learn that he needs to be more socially inclined to survive on the path he has chosen, but that remains to be seen. The trouble would be convincing him of that fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have an Abyssal of undetermined Deathlord as an enemy, if you want to use that to tie backgrounds together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T20:18:33-08:00","id":407321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=407258#post407258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have an Abyssal of undetermined Deathlord as an enemy, if you want to use that to tie backgrounds together.</div> </div> </div> </div>As in we could both have a shared opponent in a rival Deathknight that serves the Bishop, or I would be the the enemy that your background mentions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T20:22:28-08:00","id":407328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=406725#post406725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It shouldn't be a problem right off the bat.<br /> <br /> Don't the road though, who's to say.</div> </div> </div> </div>My Lunar will be doing his damnedest to keep Merciful pointed towards the Fae, if only to fulfill his goal of killing all of the Winter Folk Forever. I doubt this will get to anything beyond bickering over the campfire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T20:27:33-08:00","id":407331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Belkra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=407321#post407321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As in we could both have a shared opponent in a rival Deathknight that serves the Bishop, or I would be the the enemy that your background mentions?</div> </div> </div> </div>More the first, as written the enemy really wants me dead since I started the war that they &quot;died&quot; in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T20:42:02-08:00","id":407337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=406635#post406635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the exact words Dietaku answered me when I asked about that in a PM.<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Dietaku: We can handle it the same way Modern does. Whenever you want to alter your charm layouts or raise your essence, your body goes dormant and the exaltation rebuilds itself in a new and stronger form/ altered magical circuit layout in the case of charms. If anyone asks, , it could be an alteration caused by the Elsewhere accident that your character went through.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> I focused my character on a crafting because he arrived to creation with the clothes on his back and he was working in a laboratory. If you want to have a magitech engineer on your ship in case it breaks down or arm it I'm your guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat! I've already got a mechanic, but Grandpa Ragnar, while very experienced, is still a mortal. Plus he's getting on in years, so we could use an extra pair of hands. Fair warning, Nergui is pretty loyal to the Haslanti League, and finding an artificer like your character is pretty much a jackpot as far as they're concerned. They're probably gonna be a little more interested in exploiting you than helping you get home...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T21:36:46-08:00","id":407380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=407331#post407331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More the first, as written the enemy really wants me dead since I started the war that they &quot;died&quot; in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I could go with that. We could say that there was a time in the past where Merciful stepped in and saved the Abyssal's bacon when this other Abyssal was attempting to bring him back to the Bishop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I play forum games! Come check out the (mis?)adventures of<br /> Jensven Vargsmed and his canine companion, Shadow in &quot;Forging a Nation&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/44513-ooc-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/54288-ic-exalted-2-5-forging-a-nation\" target=\"_blank\"> IC</a>)<br /> ...or the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/w82hi22ad33hanu/Necro.doc?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Prodigal of Ashen Remorse</a> in &quot;Emerald Labyrinth&quot; (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/402616-ooc-exalted-2-5-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/416995-ic-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1146-belkra","name":"Belkra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1146_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T21:46:59-08:00","id":407386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=407337#post407337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neat! I've already got a mechanic, but Grandpa Ragnar, while very experienced, is still a mortal. Plus he's getting on in years, so we could use an extra pair of hands. Fair warning, Nergui is pretty loyal to the Haslanti League, and finding an artificer like your character is pretty much a jackpot as far as they're concerned. They're probably gonna be a little more interested in exploiting you than helping you get home...</div> </div> </div> </div>There shouldn't be any problem then my character is in an unknown world and if he wants to get home he needs friend with ressources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T02:24:16-08:00","id":407530,"title":"","content":"Well, I was gonna have a background for my character written tonight....but then I found out someone made a pilot for a Wheel of Time TV show and now I'm too angry to write anything.<br /> <br /> I'll try to get something tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T22:08:43-08:00","id":408613,"title":"","content":"Alright, I finished up one of my favorite concepts for an Exalted character: Orca, the Firedust Hurricane<br /> <br /> Backstory/Physical Description: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GGxqm7_IDUCjsTMbW7s-h-HT5v6jjMEGt5n-mQhuBkc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Character Sheet: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B__Rw-aKEixjaVFyVDNUZ1UzbjQ/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B__...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Orca doesn't have too many Intimacies because he hasn't been in the North too long. If I think of any more, I'll certainly add them and edit the link.<br /> <br /> He's also in the OOC thread.<br /> <br /> Constructive criticism is greatly appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":814,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","user":"dreamking89","date":". 02-17-2015, 02:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T08:42:45-08:00","id":410129,"title":"","content":"Okay, I have to admit, Orca's title is probably the coolest Exalted name I've seen thus far. Props to you, Dreamking. <br /> <br /> I must apologize. My compiter just up and died a few days ago. I'm posting off an far older laptop I have, and its getting a bit <br /> <br /> As for Belkra's earlier question about the Tyrant, I recognize that you and Exthalion are probably going to use the Bishop, but I'd like to add this as well, just so you all can see it. <br /> <br /> The Glacial Tyrant of Unfettered Disaster is an anomaly among the ranks of the Deathlords. She has a penchant for pomp, high technology and overwhelming force, but she has been silent for several centuries. She loves massive super-weapons the likes of which have not been seen since the First Age, but the only traces of her seem to be elite, highly trained teams of ghosts. <br /> <br /> Appearing as a short, redheaded woman with a trio of scars down her face and an aquiline nose, the Tyrant isn't what one would call conventionally attractive, but she has a unique charisma that makes most deathknights amenible to her. Indeed, she gives all who wish to join her cause a thorough education and understanding of military tactics and strategy, with her deathknights being drilled in gunshoza and airship tactics, despite neither of those items being in regular use in the Age of Sorrows. That being said, once training is over and the grandiose ranks are given, the Tyrant is extraordinarily lenient in the activities of her deathknights, allowing them free reign and great use of resources. However, one thing she does not abide by is failure, which prompts unusual and cruel torments for the lapse in trust the deathknight has earned. <br /> <br /> While the engine of war the Tyrant has grown is steady in production, the Tower of Unending Ice, her personal forge-fortress, has not been up to her expectations for some time, with the lack of a steady stream of soulsteel impeding her efforts to making the weapons she desires. While she has come up with several solutions, like chipping frozen Hekatonkhires out of the glaciers of frozen prayer around her forge and running plasmic garment racketeering rings to ensare gullible ghosts into her clutches, even this is not enough for the megalomaniacal military genius. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T09:18:33-08:00","id":410164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/400842-recruitment-exalted-2-5-the-emerald-labyrinth?p=410129#post410129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I have to admit, Orca's title is probably the coolest Exalted name I've seen thus far. Props to you, Dreamking.<br /> <br /> I must apologize. My compiter just up and died a few days ago. I'm posting off an far older laptop I have, and its getting a bit<br /> <br /> As for Belkra's earlier question about the Tyrant, I recognize that you and Exthalion are probably going to use the Bishop, but I'd like to add this as well, just so you all can see it.<br /> <br /> The Glacial Tyrant of Unfettered Disaster is an anomaly among the ranks of the Deathlords. She has a penchant for pomp, high technology and overwhelming force, but she has been silent for several centuries. She loves massive super-weapons the likes of which have not been seen since the First Age, but t